WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.520
The A to Z of isms... relativism.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.640
Moral relativism is the view that
what's right in one culture

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.080
may be wrong in another,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.840
and that there's no way of judging
between the two - it's all relative.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.320
There's no absolute truth
of the matter.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.080
Different strokes
for different folks -

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.480
and that's OK.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.520
Imagine a Martian landing on Earth -

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.800
she would see that people behave
differently in different places.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.080
They've got different moral rules,
different social customs.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.400
What's right in one location
is wrong in another.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.520
She might well conclude

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.440
that there's no such thing
as 'the right way to live'

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.680
or the 'right thing to do'
for everyone at all times.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.680
It's all a matter of cultural norms.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.840
So in parts of Spain,
bullfighting is seen as a spectacle,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.640
whereas in many other countries
it's considered outrageous cruelty.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.760
Try setting up a bull ring in
present-day London, for instance.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.560
If the visiting Martian could get an
overview of the history of the world,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.640
she'd see that
in Ancient Rome it was fine

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:03.160
to have gladiatorial combat
to the death and to own slaves,

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.480
but that both practices
would be widely frowned upon

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:06.920
in present-day Rome.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.080
Or Amsterdam. Or elsewhere.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.520
Attending fights to the death
and keeping slaves

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.400
was acceptable for the Romans,
but would be wrong in today's Europe.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.160
This sort of relativism has been
popular with some anthropologists,

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.200
who've attempted to appreciate
other cultures from within,

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.680
understanding sets
of interwoven practices

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.440
as responses to particular
circumstances and traditions.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.080
They recognise that morality
is different in different cultures,

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.240
and they often argue
that it's ethnocentric

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.480
to impose your own set of values
elsewhere, as if you know best.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.160
Such non-judgmental relativism
might seem attractive,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.640
but think about Nazi Germany.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.640
There it became socially acceptable,
and even required,

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:54.400
to treat Jews, homosexuals,
and Gypsies as less than human.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.160
This became 'right' there,
both legally and morally.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.000
A relativist would simply
have to bite the bullet,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.760
and say that that was indeed
'right' for Nazi Germany -

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.440
that's what morality meant there -

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.800
and that a morality which treats
everybody with equal respect

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.000
is no better or worse than
the Nazi way of doing things -

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.080
just different.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.320
Unless you want to embrace that
sort of repugnant conclusion,

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.480
it's probably best to steer clear
of moral relativism.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.960
Some people go further, and say that
everything is relative, even truth.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.080
That what is true at one time
and one place

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.120
isn't true for everyone everywhere.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.040
Or that there's no such thing
as objective truth,

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.600
just the truth according to me.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.080
We see hints of this
in politics today.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:38.400
There is a big problem
with this sort of relativism though,

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.400
the theory of relativism itself
would have to, on its own account,

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.680
be relative.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.200
So the theory that truth is relative
couldn't be absolutely true.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:55.040
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

